WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:19.111
The wheels of the cart continued to sink in the muddy alley.

2
00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:25.117
The old man, Fauchelevent, was still trapped under the wheels, and Mayor Madeleine was struggling to lift the

3
00:00:25.157 --> 00:00:28.640
cart. Everyone in the crowd was breathless with suspense.

4
00:00:29.224 --> 00:00:34.606
And then the cart began to rise slowly, its wheels coming half out of the ruts.

5
00:00:35.546 --> 00:00:36.766
"Help! Quickly!"

6
00:00:37.126 --> 00:00:37.927
cried Madeleine.

7
00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:42.328
Inspired by Madeleine's amazing strength, ten men rushed forward.

8
00:00:43.368 --> 00:00:46.809
Together they lifted the cart, and Fauchelevent was saved!

9
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.610
Everyone was weeping with relief now.

10
00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.731
The mayor stood up, pale and dripping with sweat.

11
00:00:53.191 --> 00:00:55.552
His clothes were torn and covered with mud.

12
00:00:56.616 --> 00:01:01.960
He looked up and saw Javert, the police inspector, staring at him, but that didn't disturb him.

13
00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:06.143
Fauchelevent had broken his knee and was in need of medical care.

14
00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:12.867
Madeleine had established an infirmary for his factory workers in his home, so that is where Fauchelevent was

15
00:01:12.907 --> 00:01:19.072
taken. When the old man woke up the next morning, he found money on the bedside table.

16
00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:24.916
There was also a note from Mayor Madeleine, saying that he had purchased Fauchelevent's cart and horse.

17
00:01:25.568 --> 00:01:30.091
The cart was broken and the horse was dead, so they were of no use to anyone.

18
00:01:31.052 --> 00:01:34.595
Buying them was not the only kind thing that the mayor did for Fauchelevent.

19
00:01:35.435 --> 00:01:38.838
After Fauchelevent got well, he had difficulty finding work.

20
00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:43.041
The mayor found a job for him as a gardener at a convent in Paris.

21
00:01:44.282 --> 00:01:47.564
Meanwhile Javert continued to be suspicious of the mayor.

22
00:01:48.164 --> 00:01:52.928
He was always respectful when he encountered Madeleine, but he avoided the man as much as possible.

23
00:01:53.948 --> 00:01:58.229
Life went on for Javert and the other inhabitants of this small French city.

24
00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:03.591
For one young woman named Fantine, the city was about to become her home again.

25
00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:08.852
At this moment Fantine was entering the town of Montfermeil near Paris.

26
00:02:09.592 --> 00:02:12.793
She was carrying her daughter, Cosette, and a heavy carpetbag.

27
00:02:14.114 --> 00:02:19.115
Cosette, who was sleeping in her mother's arms, was the prettiest little girl that you could imagine.

28
00:02:20.015 --> 00:02:24.758
She was almost three years old, and her clothes were trimmed with ribbons and lace.

29
00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:30.642
In contrast, Fantine had the appearance of a working woman seeking to return to the life of a

30
00:02:30.682 --> 00:02:33.724
peasant. Her clothes were drab and plain.

31
00:02:34.285 --> 00:02:37.267
Her face was pale, and she looked weary and sick.

32
00:02:38.327 --> 00:02:40.649
In Paris, Fantine had lived a gay life.

33
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:46.233
She was charming and beautiful, renowned for her thick blond hair and straight white teeth.

34
00:02:47.134 --> 00:02:50.176
But hard times fell upon her after she met a young man.

35
00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.482
Fantine thought they were in love—until he abandoned her.

36
00:02:55.383 --> 00:02:57.924
Soon afterward she discovered that she was pregnant.

37
00:02:59.065 --> 00:03:01.786
For a while Fantine managed to take care of her daughter.

38
00:03:02.267 --> 00:03:07.490
She stopped wearing the latest fashions and used the trimmings from her old clothes to decorate those of

39
00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:13.773
Cosette. But now at the age of 22, Fantine was desperate because she was running out of money.

40
00:03:15.134 --> 00:03:18.076
She began to think of returning to the city where she had grown up.

41
00:03:18.656 --> 00:03:21.057
Perhaps someone would remember her and give her work.

42
00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:23.778
So she sold everything she owned.

43
00:03:24.399 --> 00:03:27.880
When all her debts were paid, she had only eighty francs left.

44
00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:32.802
She had nothing in the world except her child, and she was going to have to give up

45
00:03:32.842 --> 00:03:39.745
Cosette. Fantine's heart ached, but she knew that no one would hire a woman with an illegitimate child.

46
00:03:40.606 --> 00:03:46.468
As she trudged into the town of Montfermeil, she spotted a charming scene outside an inn.

47
00:03:46.488 --> 00:03:50.011
A mother was sitting on the stone steps watching her two daughters at play.

48
00:03:50.811 --> 00:03:53.133
One was a rosy blonde and the other a brunette.

49
00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:58.777
The younger girl appeared to be about 18 months old while her sister was a year older.

50
00:03:59.377 --> 00:04:01.599
Their mother was a brawny red-haired woman.

51
00:04:01.619 --> 00:04:05.741
"You have two pretty children, Madame," Fantine said to the woman.

52
00:04:05.761 --> 00:04:07.703
"Thank you.

53
00:04:08.203 --> 00:04:11.365
I'm Madame Thenardier and my husband is the innkeeper.

54
00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:13.867
Why don't you sit by me and rest for a while?

55
00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:15.028
What brings you here?"

56
00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:21.043
Fantine sat on the steps and began to tell her story, which she changed slightly to make it

57
00:04:21.163 --> 00:04:21.964
more appealing.

58
00:04:23.164 --> 00:04:26.206
She said that she was a working woman and that her husband had died.

59
00:04:26.846 --> 00:04:31.749
Unable to find work in Paris, she was on her way to her hometown to look for employment.

60
00:04:32.630 --> 00:04:35.011
"My daughter walked a little," said Fantine.

61
00:04:35.031 --> 00:04:38.613
"But then I had to carry her, and the little jewel fell asleep."

62
00:04:39.754 --> 00:04:43.456
With those words, she gave Cosette a big kiss, which woke up the child.

63
00:04:44.192 --> 00:04:46.893
Cosette opened her big blue eyes and looked around.

64
00:04:47.893 --> 00:04:51.574
Spying the other two girls, she wiggled out of her mother's arms and ran to them.

65
00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:55.895
While the three girls played together, the two mothers talked.

66
00:04:55.915 --> 00:04:58.616
"What is your child's name?"

67
00:04:58.996 --> 00:05:00.196
asked Madame Thenardier.

68
00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:03.117
"Cosette. She's almost three years old."

69
00:05:03.137 --> 00:05:06.078
"The same age as my older daughter, Eponine.

70
00:05:06.758 --> 00:05:08.298
My younger girl is Azelma.

71
00:05:08.779 --> 00:05:11.399
Look at the three of them playing so nicely together.

72
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.540
You'd swear they were sisters."

73
00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.902
Hearing those words, Fantine suddenly thought of a solution to her problem.

74
00:05:18.402 --> 00:05:22.564
She seized Madame Thenardier's hand and said, "Will you keep my child for me?"

75
00:05:23.505 --> 00:05:26.226
Madame Thenardier looked surprised but she said nothing.

76
00:05:26.246 --> 00:05:31.489
"You see, I cannot take my child with me to the country," continued Fantine.

77
00:05:31.509 --> 00:05:34.331
"With a child, I wouldn't be able to find work.

78
00:05:34.811 --> 00:05:39.193
The sight of your little ones, so pretty and clean and happy, has overwhelmed me.

79
00:05:40.294 --> 00:05:43.456
I can tell that you're a good mother and that they'll be like three sisters.

80
00:05:44.692 --> 00:05:46.613
It won't be long until I can come back for Cosette.

81
00:05:46.673 --> 00:05:47.934
Please keep her for me?"

82
00:05:47.954 --> 00:05:52.016
"I must think it over," said Madame Thenardier.

83
00:05:52.036 --> 00:05:53.997
"I'll give you six francs a month."

84
00:05:54.838 --> 00:05:58.499
"Make it seven francs," said a man's voice from within the inn.

85
00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.681
"And six months paid in advance."

86
00:06:00.701 --> 00:06:04.283
"That's my husband," said Madame Thenardier.

87
00:06:04.303 --> 00:06:07.524
"Seven francs times six months would be forty-two francs."

88
00:06:08.525 --> 00:06:14.008
"Plus 15 francs for any additional expenses," said Monsieur Thenardier from the interior of the inn again.

89
00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.461
"I'll give you 57 francs," said Fantine.

90
00:06:17.481 --> 00:06:21.642
"I have eighty francs, so that will leave me enough to get to the country if I walk.

91
00:06:22.522 --> 00:06:25.943
I'll earn some money there, and as soon as I can, I'll come back for my little love."

92
00:06:26.743 --> 00:06:28.164
"Does the child have clothing?"

93
00:06:28.524 --> 00:06:29.704
asked Monsieur Thenardier.

94
00:06:29.724 --> 00:06:33.165
"Of course she does, the poor darling," said Fantine.

95
00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:39.447
"It's an extravagant wardrobe too, with clothes by the dozens and silk dresses like a lady.

96
00:06:39.907 --> 00:06:41.147
It's all in my carpetbag."

97
00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:45.221
"Then I think we can keep her," said Monsieur Thenardier.

98
00:06:46.082 --> 00:06:50.205
Fantine spent the night at the inn, and the next morning she left for the country.

99
00:06:51.046 --> 00:06:53.348
A neighbor of the Thenardiers saw her on the road.

100
00:06:53.368 --> 00:06:58.992
"I've just passed a woman crying as if her heart would break," he said when he stopped at

101
00:06:59.012 --> 00:06:59.333
the inn.

102
00:06:59.353 --> 00:07:00.894
"I wonder what was wrong."

103
00:07:00.914 --> 00:07:07.700
"I have no idea," said Monsieur Thenardier, touching the 57 francs in his pocket.

104
00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.981
He had a debt that was due that day.

105
00:07:10.802 --> 00:07:15.224
Fantine's money would give him enough to pay it and keep seven francs for himself.
